      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_aligned_alloc",
      "summary": "Test k_heap_aligned_alloc() API usage and edge cases."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-alloc-pending",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "In main thread alloc a buffer from the heap, then run the child thread. If there isn't enough space in the heap, the child thread will wait timeout long until main thread free the buffer to heap.\n\n*See also:* k_heap_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_heap_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_pending"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_pending",
      "summary": "Validate the k_heap support wait between different threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-alloc-pending-null",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "In main thread alloc two buffer from the heap, then run the child thread which alloc a buffer larger than remaining space. The child thread will wait timeout long until main thread free one of the buffer to heap, space in the heap is still not enough and then return null after timeout.\n\n*See also:* k_heap_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_heap_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_pending_null"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_pending_null",
      "summary": "Validate the k_heap alloc_pending_null support."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-alloc-size",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Parameterized over a range of block sizes: sizes within HEAP_SIZE must allocate successfully and survive a write/read-back of a fill pattern; sizes beyond heap capacity must return NULL. Each (size, expectation) pair is reported as a separate named Twister case, so a failure pinpoints the exact size rather than a single aggregate result.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Read the current (size, expect_success) parameter pair.\n- Call k_heap_alloc() for that size.\n- On a success case: assert non-NULL, write a per-byte pattern, read it back to confirm no corruption, then free the block.\n- On a failure case: assert the call returned NULL.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- In-capacity sizes allocate, preserve data, and free cleanly.\n- Over-capacity sizes return NULL.\n\n*See also:* k_heap_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_heap_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_size"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_alloc_size",
      "summary": "Verify k_heap_alloc() succeeds within capacity and fails beyond it."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-array-get",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test ensures that valid values are returned\n\n*See also:* k_heap_array_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_array_get"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_array_get",
      "summary": "Test k_heap_array_get()."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-calloc",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test allocates 256 unsigned integers of 4 bytes for a total of 1024 bytes from the 2048 byte heap. It checks if allocation and initialization are successful or not. Also tests k_heap_calloc() overflow and zero-size edge cases\n\n*See also:* k_heap_calloc(), k_heap_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_calloc"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_calloc",
      "summary": "Test k_heap_calloc() and k_heap_free() API usage."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-free",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test validates k_heap_free() API, by using below steps\n\n- allocate the memory from the heap,\n- free a NULL pointer (should have no effect)\n- free the allocated memory\n- allocate memory more than the first allocation. The allocation in the 4th step should succeed if k_heap_free() works as expected\n\n*See also:* k_heap_alloc, k_heap_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_free"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_free",
      "summary": "Test k_heap_free() API functionality."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-init",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Initialize a k_heap at run time over a caller-provided memory buffer with k_heap_init(), then confirm the heap is usable: a block can be allocated (and the returned memory lies within the provided region and is writable), an allocation larger than the region fails, and the block can be freed.\n\n*See also:* k_heap_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_init"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_init",
      "summary": "Test initializing a memory heap at run time over a provided region."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-min-size",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Create a minimum size (1-byte) static heap, verify that it works to allocate that byte at runtime and that it doesn't overflow its memory bounds.\n\n*See also:* K_HEAP_DEFINE()\n\n*See also:* k_heap_alloc()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_min_size"
        }
      ],
      "name": "k_heap_api__test_k_heap_min_size",
      "summary": "Test a minimum-size static k_heap."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/k-heap-api--test-k-heap-realloc",
