      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-malloc-in-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "When a thread's resource pool is not assigned, alloc memory will fail.\n\n*See also:* z_thread_malloc()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_malloc_in_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_malloc_in_thread",
      "summary": "Validate allocation and free failure when thread's resource pool is not assigned."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-mheap-calloc",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test validates k_calloc() API. When requesting a huge size of space or a space larger than heap memory, the API will return NULL. The 8 blocks of memory of size 16 bytes are allocated by k_calloc() API. When allocated using k_calloc() the memory buffers have to be zeroed. Check is done, if the blocks are memset to 0 and read/write is allowed. The test is then teared up by freeing all the blocks allocated.\n\n*See also:* k_calloc()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_mheap_calloc"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_mheap_calloc",
      "summary": "Test to demonstrate k_calloc() API functionality."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-mheap-malloc-align4",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The 8 blocks of memory of size 16 bytes are allocated by k_calloc() API. When allocated using k_calloc() the memory buffers have to be zeroed. Check is done, if the blocks are memset to 0 and read/write is allowed. The test is then teared up by freeing all the blocks allocated.\n\n*See also:* k_malloc(), k_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_mheap_malloc_align4"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_mheap_malloc_align4",
      "summary": "The test validates k_calloc() API."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-mheap-malloc-free",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test allocates 4 blocks from heap memory pool using k_malloc() API. It also tries to allocate a block of size 64 bytes which fails as all the memory is allocated up. It then validates k_free() API by freeing up all the blocks which were allocated from the heap memory.\n\n*See also:* k_malloc()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_mheap_malloc_free"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_mheap_malloc_free",
      "summary": "Test to demonstrate k_malloc() and k_free() API usage."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-mheap-realloc",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The test resizes blocks previously allocated from the system heap with k_realloc(), growing and shrinking allocations and verifying the contents are preserved and that allocation back to the system heap works.\n\n*See also:* k_realloc()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_mheap_realloc"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_mheap_realloc",
      "summary": "Test to demonstrate k_realloc() API usage."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-mheap-threadsafe",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Test creates three preemptive threads of equal priority. In each child thread , call k_malloc() to alloc a block of memory. Check These four threads can share the same heap space without interfering with each other.",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_mheap_threadsafe"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_mheap_threadsafe",
      "summary": "Verify alloc from multiple equal priority threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mheap-api--test-sys-heap-mem-pool-assign",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Set heap memory as resource pool. It will success when alloc a block of memory smaller than the pool and will fail when alloc a block of memory larger than the pool.\n\n*See also:* k_thread_system_pool_assign()\n\n*See also:* z_thread_malloc()\n\n*See also:* k_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mheap_api__test_sys_heap_mem_pool_assign"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mheap_api__test_sys_heap_mem_pool_assign",
      "summary": "Validate allocation and free from system heap memory pool."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-alloc",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_msgq_alloc_init() draws its buffer from the thread's resource pool. It must succeed for a request the pool can satisfy, return -ENOMEM when the requested buffer exceeds the pool, and -EINVAL when the message size would overflow.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Alloc-init a queue that fits the pool and use it, then clean it up.\n- Request a buffer larger than the pool and expect -ENOMEM.\n- Request an overflowing message size and expect -EINVAL.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Success for a valid request; -ENOMEM and -EINVAL for the failing requests.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_cleanup()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_alloc"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_alloc",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_alloc_init() allocation success and failure paths."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-attrs-get",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_msgq_get_attrs() must reflect the live occupancy of the queue. The test reads the attributes when empty, after filling the queue to capacity, and again after draining it, confirming used_msgs tracks each transition.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Get attributes of an empty queue and verify used_msgs is 0.\n- Fill the queue and verify used_msgs equals the queue length.\n- Drain the queue and verify used_msgs is 0 again.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- used_msgs reports 0, full, then 0 as messages are added and removed.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get_attrs()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_attrs_get"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_attrs_get",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_get_attrs() reports the used-message count."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-define",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A queue created with K_MSGQ_DEFINE() must be fully initialized at boot for the size and depth given to the macro: empty, with all slots free, and immediately usable for message passing without any run-time initialization call.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Check the statically defined queue is empty with MSGQ_LEN free slots and that a peek reports no message.\n- Put a message and get it back, verifying the data round-trips.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The statically defined queue accepts and delivers messages as-is.\n\n*See also:* K_MSGQ_DEFINE",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_define"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_define",
      "summary": "Verify a message queue defined at compile time is ready for use."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-init",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_msgq_init() must set up a message queue over a caller-provided buffer for the given message size and depth: the queue starts empty, with all slots free, and is immediately usable for message passing.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Initialize a queue at run time with a caller-provided buffer.\n- Check it is empty (no used slots, all slots free, peek reports no message).\n- Put a message and get it back, verifying the data round-trips.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The initialized queue is empty and accepts and delivers messages.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_init"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_init",
      "summary": "Verify run-time initialization of a message queue."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-isr",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Messages enqueued from interrupt context (via irq_offload()) must be retrieved in thread context in FIFO order, confirming k_msgq_put() is ISR-safe. Run against both an init()ed and a K_MSGQ_DEFINE()d queue.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- From an ISR, put MSGQ_LEN messages into the queue.\n- In thread context, get them all and verify FIFO order, then purge.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The thread receives every ISR-enqueued message in order.\n\n*Note:* The kernel.message_queue.put_front scenario builds this with CONFIG_TEST_MSGQ_PUT_FRONT=y, so the ISR enqueues via k_msgq_put_front() and the thread checks the prepend (LIFO) ordering.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put_front()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_isr"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_isr",
      "summary": "Verify message passing from an ISR to a thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-peek",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_msgq_peek() must report -ENOMSG on an empty queue, return the message at the front of a non-empty queue without consuming it, and a subsequent get must return the same message that was peeked.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Peek at an empty queue and expect -ENOMSG.\n- Put two messages, peek, and verify the front message is returned and the used count is unchanged.\n- Get a message and verify it matches the peeked one.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Peek returns the front message without removing it and fails with -ENOMSG on an empty queue.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_peek()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_peek"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_peek",
      "summary": "Verify peeking reads the front message without removing it."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-peek-at",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Put two distinct messages into a message queue, then use k_msgq_peek_at() to read the message at each valid index and verify the returned values match what was enqueued, without removing them (the used count stays unchanged). Also verify that peeking at an index beyond the number of queued messages returns -ENOMSG.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_peek_at()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_peek_at"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_peek_at",
      "summary": "Test peeking at a message by index without removing it."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-put-front-order",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_msgq_put_front() inserts a message at the front of the queue, so a receiver must get it before messages that were already queued, while the messages sent to the end keep their relative order.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Put a message at the end of the queue.\n- Put a second message at the front with k_msgq_put_front().\n- Get both messages and verify the front-inserted one arrives first.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The front-inserted message is received first, the end-queued one second.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put_front()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_put_front_order"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_put_front_order",
      "summary": "Verify a front-inserted message is received before queued ones."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-thread-overflow",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "After messages have been consumed, new puts must reuse freed slots and the internal write pointer must advance (wrap) rather than reset to the buffer start. A blocked consumer and interleaved puts exercise the wrap, and the test asserts the write pointer did not return to the buffer start.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Initialize a length-2 queue and put one message.\n- Start a consumer that gets two messages, then put the second message.\n- After the exchange, verify the write pointer is not at buffer_start.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Messages pass correctly and the write pointer wraps within the ring buffer.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_thread_overflow"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_thread_overflow",
      "summary": "Verify the ring buffer wraps correctly across put/get cycles."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-attrs-get",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Same used-message accounting as test_msgq_attrs_get(), but exercised from a user-mode thread on a queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(), confirming the attribute query works under userspace with a dynamically allocated queue.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a message queue as a user thread.\n- Verify used_msgs is 0, then full, then 0 across fill/drain.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- used_msgs is reported correctly from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get_attrs()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_attrs_get"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_attrs_get",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_get_attrs() from user mode on an allocated queue."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-get-fail",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "User-mode counterpart of test_msgq_get_fail() on a queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(): an empty-queue get must return -ENOMSG (no wait) and -EAGAIN (timeout).\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a queue as a user thread.\n- Get with K_NO_WAIT (-ENOMSG) and with a finite timeout (-EAGAIN).\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The error codes match the supervisor case from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_get_fail"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_get_fail",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_get() empty-queue error codes from user mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-purge-when-put",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "User-mode counterpart of test_msgq_purge_when_put() on a queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(): purging while a writer pends must discard messages, wake the writer with -ENOMSG, and leave the queue usable.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a queue as a user thread and fill it.\n- Start a pending writer, purge, and verify recovery.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Behavior matches the supervisor case from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_purge()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_purge_when_put"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_purge_when_put",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_purge() with a pending writer from user mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-put-fail",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "User-mode counterpart of test_msgq_put_fail() on a queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(): a full-queue put must return -ENOMSG (no wait) and -EAGAIN (timeout).\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a queue as a user thread and fill it.\n- Put with K_NO_WAIT (-ENOMSG) and with a finite timeout (-EAGAIN).\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The error codes match the supervisor case from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_put_fail"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_put_fail",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_put() full-queue error codes from user mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Same FIFO data-passing contract as test_msgq_thread(), exercised from a user-mode thread on a queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(), confirming the put/get/purge flow works under userspace.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a queue as a user thread.\n- Run the producer/consumer data-passing sequence and purge.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Messages pass in order from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_thread",
      "summary": "Verify thread-to-thread message passing from user mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api--test-msgq-user-thread-overflow",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "User-mode counterpart of test_msgq_thread_overflow(): on a length-1 queue created with k_msgq_alloc_init(), interleaved puts and gets must reuse freed slots correctly from userspace.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate and alloc-init a length-1 queue as a user thread.\n- Run the overflow put/get sequence with a blocked consumer.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Messages pass correctly with buffer wrap from user mode.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_alloc_init()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_thread_overflow"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api__test_msgq_user_thread_overflow",
      "summary": "Verify ring-buffer wrap from user mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-empty",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A get on an empty queue must return -ENOMSG for K_NO_WAIT, -EAGAIN after a finite timeout, and block under K_FOREVER until a put arrives. While a thread is pending on the queue, k_msgq_cleanup() must refuse with -EBUSY.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Start a thread that gets from an empty queue with K_NO_WAIT (-ENOMSG), a finite timeout (-EAGAIN), then blocks on K_FOREVER.\n- While it is pending, call k_msgq_cleanup() and expect -EBUSY.\n- Put a message to wake the pending getter.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The get returns -ENOMSG/-EAGAIN as appropriate, cleanup returns -EBUSY, and the K_FOREVER get completes once a message is put.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_cleanup()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_empty"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_empty",
      "summary": "Verify get-from-empty timeout behavior and cleanup-while-pending."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-full",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A put on a full queue must return -ENOMSG for K_NO_WAIT, -EAGAIN after a finite timeout, and block under K_FOREVER until space becomes available.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Fill a length-1 queue, then start a thread that puts with K_NO_WAIT (-ENOMSG), a finite timeout (-EAGAIN), then blocks on K_FOREVER.\n- Confirm the thread is pending after the non-blocking attempts.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The put returns -ENOMSG/-EAGAIN as appropriate and blocks under K_FOREVER.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_full"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_full",
      "summary": "Verify put-to-full timeout behavior."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-get-fail",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "On an empty queue, a non-blocking get must return -ENOMSG and a get with a finite timeout must return -EAGAIN after the timeout elapses.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- On an empty queue, get with K_NO_WAIT and expect -ENOMSG.\n- Get with a finite timeout and expect -EAGAIN.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- k_msgq_get() returns -ENOMSG (no wait) and -EAGAIN (timeout) when empty.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_get_fail"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_get_fail",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_get() error codes when the queue is empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-pend-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "On a length-1 queue, a writer that blocks because the queue is full must be unblocked and complete its put once a reader removes a message, passing the data through to the reader.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Fill a length-1 queue, then start a writer that pends on a put.\n- Start a reader that drains the queue.\n- Confirm the pending put completes and the data is delivered, then purge.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The blocked writer is woken and its message reaches the reader.\n\n*Note:* Under the kernel.message_queue.put_front scenario (CONFIG_TEST_MSGQ_PUT_FRONT=y) the writer uses k_msgq_put_front(), which does not block: on a full queue it returns -ENOMSG instead of pending.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put_front()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_pend_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_pend_thread",
      "summary": "Verify a writer pending on a full queue is served when space frees."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-purge-when-put",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Purging a full queue must discard all queued messages and unblock any thread waiting to put, returning -ENOMSG to that writer. After the purge the queue must be usable again for new puts.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Fill the queue, then start a writer that blocks on a put with a timeout.\n- Purge the queue while the writer is pending.\n- Verify the writer's put returns -ENOMSG and the queue accepts new messages.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Purge empties the queue, the pending writer gets -ENOMSG, and the queue is usable afterwards.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_purge()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_purge_when_put"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_purge_when_put",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_purge() drops messages and wakes a pending writer."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-put-fail",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Once a queue is full, a non-blocking put must return -ENOMSG and a put with a finite timeout must return -EAGAIN after the timeout elapses.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Fill the queue, then put with K_NO_WAIT and expect -ENOMSG.\n- Put with a finite timeout and expect -EAGAIN.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- k_msgq_put() returns -ENOMSG (no wait) and -EAGAIN (timeout) when full.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_put_fail"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_put_fail",
      "summary": "Verify k_msgq_put() error codes when the queue is full."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A producer fills the queue and a consumer thread drains it; messages must be delivered in FIFO order and the occupancy counters (num_free/num_used) and k_msgq_peek() must track the contents throughout. Run against both a k_msgq_init()ed and a K_MSGQ_DEFINE()d queue.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Producer puts MSGQ_LEN messages, checking peek and free/used counts.\n- A consumer thread gets them all and verifies FIFO order.\n- Purge the queue and confirm it is empty.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- All messages are received in order and the counters stay consistent.\n\n*Note:* The kernel.message_queue.put_front scenario builds this with CONFIG_TEST_MSGQ_PUT_FRONT=y, exercising k_msgq_put_front() in place of k_msgq_put() and checking the resulting prepend (LIFO) ordering.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put_front()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_thread"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_thread",
      "summary": "Verify FIFO data passing through a message queue between two threads."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-api-1cpu--test-msgq-thread-pending",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "With a full length-2 queue, a thread attempting another put (or put_front) blocks; once the main thread drains the queue, the messages must come out in the expected order, validating that pending writers do not corrupt ordering.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Fill a length-2 queue (using put and put_front).\n- Start a thread that attempts a further prepend/put and pends.\n- Drain the queue and verify the messages are returned in the expected order.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Messages are dequeued in the correct order despite the pending writer.\n\n*Note:* The kernel.message_queue.put_front scenario (CONFIG_TEST_MSGQ_PUT_FRONT=y) fills the queue and prepends via k_msgq_put_front(), checking that a full-queue prepend returns -ENOMSG and that the front-inserted message is dequeued first.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put_front()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_thread_pending"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_api_1cpu__test_msgq_thread_pending",
      "summary": "Verify message ordering when a writer pends on a full queue."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/msgq-usage--test-msgq-usage",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Exercises message queues as the IPC backbone of a realistic service registry: a manager thread, two service threads and a client thread each own a queue and communicate by put/get to register services, query them, issue request/response calls, and tear services down (with k_msgq_purge() waking waiters). The flow must complete without loss or deadlock and the client must observe each service's running response.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Start the service manager, two services that register, and a client.\n- The client queries the manager, calls each service, and validates replies.\n- Tear down each service and join all threads.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Services register, the client receives correct responses, and all threads complete cleanly.\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_put()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_get()\n\n*See also:* k_msgq_purge()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "msgq_usage__test_msgq_usage"
        }
      ],
      "name": "msgq_usage__test_msgq_usage",
      "summary": "Verify message queues coordinate a multi-service registry scenario."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mslab-api--test-mslab-alloc-align",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Allocate 3 blocks of memory from 2 memory slabs respectively and check if all blocks are aligned to 8 bytes and free them.",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "mslab_api__test_mslab_alloc_align"
        }
      ],
      "name": "mslab_api__test_mslab_alloc_align",
      "summary": "Allocate memory blocks and check for alignment of 8 bytes."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/mslab-api--test-mslab-alloc-free-thread",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
