    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-system--test-obj-core-stats-system",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "The kernel and per-CPU object cores expose run-time statistics. This test obtains both the raw and queried statistics for these object cores and checks the expected aggregation relationships hold (per-CPU sampling is at least as large as kernel sampling, and the sum across CPUs is at least the kernel total).\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Optionally spin up a busy thread per extra CPU to generate activity.\n- Fetch raw stats for the kernel and each CPU with k_obj_core_stats_raw().\n- Fetch queried stats for the kernel and each CPU with k_obj_core_stats_query() and sum the per-CPU values.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Each call returns 0 and the per-CPU/aggregate values are no smaller than the corresponding kernel values.\n\n*See also:* k_obj_core_stats_raw()\n\n*See also:* k_obj_core_stats_query()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_system__test_obj_core_stats_system"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_system__test_obj_core_stats_system",
      "summary": "Verify run-time statistics can be queried for the kernel and CPU object cores."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/obj-core-stats-thread--test-obj-core-stats-thread-test",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Thread object cores expose query, raw, reset, enable and disable statistics operations backed by the thread run-time stats. This test drives a helper thread through known busy/blocked phases and validates the statistics interface end to end:\n\n- while the thread is blocked its stats do not change;\n- while it runs its execution/total cycles increase;\n- the object core query matches k_thread_runtime_stats_get();\n- resetting clears the counters;\n- disabling freezes the counters and re-enabling resumes collection.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Sample raw and queried stats while the helper thread is blocked, busy-wait, and confirm the samples are unchanged.\n- Let the thread run, re-sample, and confirm cycles increased and the object core query equals k_thread_runtime_stats_get().\n- Reset the stats and confirm the counters are zero.\n- Disable the stats, let the thread run, and confirm the counters are frozen.\n- Re-enable the stats, let the thread run, and confirm the counters advance.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Every operation returns 0 and the sampled statistics behave as described.\n\n*See also:* k_obj_core_stats_raw()\n\n*See also:* k_obj_core_stats_query() k_obj_core_stats_reset(), k_obj_core_stats_enable(), k_obj_core_stats_disable()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "obj_core_stats_thread__test_obj_core_stats_thread_test"
        }
      ],
      "name": "obj_core_stats_thread__test_obj_core_stats_thread_test",
      "summary": "Verify the full statistics life cycle for a thread object core."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/object-validation--test-kobj-assign-perms-on-alloc-obj",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A thread that allocates a kernel object must be able to use it straight away, without a separate grant: the allocation implicitly gives the requesting thread permission. The object also has to come out of that thread's own resource pool, so its address is checked against the pool bounds, and it is then used through an ordinary API call, which would fail the permission check if the implicit grant were missing.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate a semaphore object with k_object_alloc().\n- Check its address lies within the calling thread's resource pool.\n- Call k_sem_init() on it from the same thread.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The allocation succeeds, the object lies in the thread's pool, and the thread can initialize it without being granted access explicitly.\n\n*See also:* k_object_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_sem_init()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "object_validation__test_kobj_assign_perms_on_alloc_obj"
        }
      ],
      "name": "object_validation__test_kobj_assign_perms_on_alloc_obj",
      "summary": "Verify that allocating an object grants the caller permission on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/object-validation--test-kobj-freed-when-unreferenced",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "For a dynamically allocated object the set of threads holding permission on it doubles as its reference count, so revoking the last permission has to release the memory rather than leak it. The object is looked up again afterwards, and its disappearance from the object table is what shows the release happened.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Allocate a mutex object with k_object_alloc().\n- Revoke the allocating thread's access, leaving no thread with permission.\n- Look the object up and validate it.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The object is no longer in the table, reported as -EBADF, so its memory was released.\n\n*See also:* k_object_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_object_access_revoke()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "object_validation__test_kobj_freed_when_unreferenced"
        }
      ],
      "name": "object_validation__test_kobj_freed_when_unreferenced",
      "summary": "Verify that a kernel object is freed once nothing references it."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/object-validation--test-kobj-validate-states",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Every system call that takes a kernel object has to answer three questions about it before trusting it: is this address a kernel object at all, does the calling thread have access to it, and is it initialized and of the expected type. Each answer has its own error code, so the test drives an address through every state in turn unknown to the table, known but not granted, granted but uninitialized, and fully usable and checks the code that comes back. Dynamically allocated objects are put through the same sequence and then freed, which also covers an object leaving the table.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Validate a stack variable, a bad address and a wild pointer, none of which are in the object table.\n- Validate static objects with and without permission granted, before and after initialization.\n- Allocate objects at run time, granting an extra reference so they survive revocation, and validate them through the same states.\n- Free each dynamic object and validate it once more.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Addresses outside the table report -EBADF, objects without permission or not yet initialized report -EINVAL, usable objects validate successfully, and a freed object goes back to reporting -EBADF.\n\n*See also:* k_object_alloc()\n\n*See also:* k_object_access_grant()\n\n*See also:* k_object_free()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "object_validation__test_kobj_validate_states"
        }
      ],
      "name": "object_validation__test_kobj_validate_states",
      "summary": "Verify that kernel object validation reports address, permission, type and init state."
    },
    {
