    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sleep--test-sleep",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A cooperative test thread performs a sequence of one-second sleeps while a helper thread, an ISR (via irq_offload()) and the main thread each wake it early. The test validates both the timekeeping and the cancellation paths of the sleep primitives:\n\n- An uncancelled k_sleep() must block for at least the requested duration and no more than one tick of slop.\n- A k_wakeup() targeting a sleeping thread must return it to the ready queue without waiting for the timeout to expire, regardless of whether the wakeup originates from a thread, an ISR, or the main thread.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Create a cooperative test thread and a higher-priority helper thread.\n- Let the test thread run one uncancelled k_sleep(K_SECONDS(1)) and confirm the elapsed time matches the request within TICK_MARGIN.\n- Have the helper thread, an irq_offload() ISR, and the main thread each call k_wakeup() on the test thread mid-sleep and confirm each sleep returns within TICK_MARGIN.\n- Run one final uncancelled k_sleep() on the main thread and validate its duration.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Uncancelled sleeps elapse for the requested duration (within slop).\n- Every k_wakeup() cancels the sleep promptly and test_failure stays false.\n\n*See also:* k_sleep()\n\n*See also:* k_wakeup()\n\n*See also:* k_uptime_get_32()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sleep__test_sleep"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sleep__test_sleep",
      "summary": "Verify that k_sleep() sleeps for the requested time and that k_wakeup() cancels a pending sleep immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sleep--test-sleep-forever",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A user-mode thread calls k_sleep(K_FOREVER), which must never expire on its own. The thread only becomes runnable again after the main thread issues a k_wakeup(). On return, k_sleep() must report K_TICKS_FOREVER to indicate the sleep was cancelled rather than timed out.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Create a user-mode thread that calls k_sleep(K_FOREVER).\n- Yield so the thread reaches the sleeping state.\n- Call k_wakeup() on the thread from the main thread.\n- In the woken thread, assert the return value equals K_TICKS_FOREVER.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The thread stays asleep until woken and k_sleep() returns K_TICKS_FOREVER.\n\n*See also:* k_sleep()\n\n*See also:* k_wakeup()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sleep__test_sleep_forever"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sleep__test_sleep_forever",
      "summary": "Verify that k_sleep(K_FOREVER) blocks until an explicit wakeup and returns K_TICKS_FOREVER."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sleep--test-sleep-wakeup-returns-remaining",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Put a thread to sleep for a long, finite duration and wake it with k_wakeup() before that duration elapses. k_sleep() must return the amount of time that was still remaining, which is non-zero and does not exceed the originally requested duration.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Start a thread that sleeps for 10 seconds and stores k_sleep()'s return.\n- Yield so the thread begins sleeping, let ~100 ms pass, then wake it with k_wakeup().\n- Inspect the stored return value.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- k_sleep() returns a value greater than zero and less than the requested 10000 ms, i.e. it reports the time that was still remaining.\n\n*See also:* k_sleep()\n\n*See also:* k_wakeup()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sleep__test_sleep_wakeup_returns_remaining"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sleep__test_sleep_wakeup_returns_remaining",
      "summary": "Verify k_sleep() reports the remaining time when woken early."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/sleep--test-usleep",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Absolute microsecond sleep durations cannot be validated portably because the granularity of k_usleep() depends on the tick rate and timer hardware. Instead, this test issues k_usleep(1) in a loop sized to span one second of ticks and checks that the aggregate elapsed time stays within a computed lower and upper bound. This proves that each minimal sleep rounds up to at least the tick period (never returns early) while remaining bounded above by the per-iteration alignment overhead. Because precise timing is unreliable under emulation, the measurement is retried up to RETRIES times and passes if any iteration lands in range.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Record the uptime, then call k_usleep(1) for LOOPS iterations.\n- Compute the elapsed time and compare it against LOWER_BOUND_MS and UPPER_BOUND_MS, retrying the whole measurement up to RETRIES times.\n- Assert the elapsed time is neither below the lower bound (short sleep) nor above the upper bound (overslept).\n\nExpected result:\n\n- Total elapsed time is within [LOWER_BOUND_MS, UPPER_BOUND_MS], confirming k_usleep() sleeps for at least the minimal granularity and no longer than the expected alignment overhead.\n\n*See also:* k_usleep()\n\n*See also:* k_uptime_get()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "sleep__test_usleep"
        }
      ],
      "name": "sleep__test_usleep",
      "summary": "Verify that k_usleep() never sleeps for less than the minimum tick granularity."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/stack-contexts--test-stack-alloc-null",
