      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "A stack created with K_STACK_DEFINE() must be fully initialized at boot: empty and immediately usable without any run-time initialization call. Push an item onto the statically defined stack and pop it back, verifying the value round-trips.\n\n*See also:* K_STACK_DEFINE(x), k_stack_push(), k_stack_pop()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "stack_contexts__test_stack_define"
        }
      ],
      "name": "stack_contexts__test_stack_define",
      "summary": "Verify a stack defined at compile time is ready for use."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/stack-contexts--test-stack-init",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "k_stack_init() must set up a stack over a caller-provided memory area with the given capacity: the stack starts empty (a non-blocking pop fails) and accepts and returns items.\n\n*See also:* k_stack_init(), k_stack_push(), k_stack_pop()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "stack_contexts__test_stack_init"
        }
      ],
      "name": "stack_contexts__test_stack_init",
      "summary": "Verify run-time initialization of a stack over a caller buffer."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/stack-contexts--test-stack-multithread-competition",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Define three threads, and set a higher priority for two of them, and set a lower priority for the last one. Then Add a delay between creating the two high priority threads. Test point:\n\n- Any number of threads may wait(K_FOREVER set) on an empty stack simultaneously.\n- When data is pushed, it is given to the highest priority thread that has waited longest.",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "stack_contexts__test_stack_multithread_competition"
        }
      ],
      "name": "stack_contexts__test_stack_multithread_competition",
      "summary": "Test multi-threads to get data from stack."
    },
    {
