      "summary": "Verify submitting a work item to a started queue runs its handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/work-1cpu--test-1cpu-suspend-resume-queue",
      "functionalsafety_verificationMethod": [
        "spdx:FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test"
      ],
      "creationInfo": "zephyr:creationinfo",
      "description": "Work submitted while the work queue's thread is suspended must be accepted and stay queued, not lost or rejected, and must run as soon as the thread is resumed.\n\nTest steps:\n\n- Look up the queue's thread with k_work_queue_thread_get() and suspend it.\n- Submit a work item and verify it is accepted and reported as queued.\n- Sleep and verify the item has not run and is still pending.\n- Resume the queue thread.\n\nExpected result:\n\n- The handler runs exactly once after the resume, and the item ends idle.\n\n*See also:* k_work_submit_to_queue()\n\n*See also:* k_work_queue_thread_get()\n\n*See also:* k_thread_suspend()\n\n*See also:* k_thread_resume()",
      "externalIdentifier": [
        {
          "type": "ExternalIdentifier",
          "comment": "ztest case",
          "externalIdentifierType": "other",
          "identifier": "work_1cpu__test_1cpu_suspend_resume_queue"
        }
      ],
      "name": "work_1cpu__test_1cpu_suspend_resume_queue",
      "summary": "Verify work submitted while the queue thread is suspended runs on resume."
    },
    {
      "type": "functionalsafety_RequirementVerification",
      "spdxId": "zephyr:verifications/work-1cpu--test-1cpu-sync-queue",
